The licence above covers this repository's own files: the program around
TIC-80 (waterbox/), the patches, the tests and the documents.

TIC-80 (extern/tic80, a submodule) is Vadim Grigoruk's and its authors',
also under the MIT licence (extern/tic80/LICENSE). It carries the
programming languages it runs and the libraries it uses, each under its own
licence, listed in extern/tic80/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. All of them are
permissive except blip_buf, the sound resampler, which is under the GNU
Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later.

The package this repository builds carries every one of those licence texts
(waterbox/package-licenses.json says which). It contains no cart of anyone's.
